sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Mongera et al. (2018) & Kim et al. (2021) zebrafish tailbud active fluid-to-solid jamming transition & yield-stress axis elongation — MorphoEval overall 91.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py` (91.3/100, up from 57.3/100 in Pass 1; +34.0 points). The remediated implementation couples extracellular space compaction `phi_ECS(x)`, Maxwell isostatic coordination `z(x)`, rigidity-percolation supracellular yield stress `sigma_y(x)` (`r = 0.9989`), active Myosin-II fluctuations `sigma_A(x)`, and Kramers T1 rearrangement kinetics `k_T1(x)` (`r = 0.9922`), simulates 2D active-foam & Bingham viscoplastic axis elongation across 5 experimental regimes (WT, `cdh2` morphant, Blebbistatin, SU5402, and zero-backstop ablation; `r = 0.9717` for elongation velocity and `r = 0.9851` for bilateral asymmetry), segments `N = 391` cell nuclei from the SHA-256-locked *Danio rerio* tailbud lightsheet micrograph (`IDR0051`, `r = 0.9915`), and is backed by 4 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_030_neuromesodermal_jamming.lean`. Overall 91.4/100 (faithfulness 90.9, reproducibility 92.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0cb0132; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/neuromesodermal_jamming_comparison.png: rendered output of 2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py at 0cb0132, image/png, 732687 B, 3150×1320 px, artifact_sha256 de989cdbda2538b3ac78b567588057367c51e4f73aa8cca93a923398e4b1e838 (sha256 de989cdbda2538b3ac78b567588057367c51e4f73aa8cca93a923398e4b1e838), spec_fingerprint 5225f2c29acda8d1ee81d082219556f85a1159006d552c629f56ce7d8a842027. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 5225f2c29acda8d1ee81d082219556f85a1159006d552c629f56ce7d8a842027; artifact_sha256: de989cdbda2538b3ac78b567588057367c51e4f73aa8cca93a923398e4b1e838. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-neuromesodermal-jamming-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Mongera et al. (2018) Nature 561:401-405 Figs. 1-4: along the posterior-to-anterior axis of the zebrafish tailbud, extracellular space fraction phi_ECS(x) decreases from ~14.5% in the posterior Mesodermal Progenitor Zone (MPZ) to ~4.9% in the Anterior Presomitic Mesoderm (A-PSM), driving cell packing phi_pack = 1 - phi_ECS across the rigidity-percolation threshold phi_c approx 0.860 and elevating ferrofluid-measured yield stress sigma_y(x) from ~11 Pa to ~118 Pa while active Myosin-II tension fluctuations sigma_A(x) decline from ~50 Pa to ~13 Pa. | Kim et al. (2021) Nature Physics 17:859-866 & Mongera et al. (2018) Fig. 4: active tension fluctuations fluidize the MPZ (sigma_A > sigma_y) via frequent T1 neighbor exchanges, whereas the jammed solid A-PSM (sigma_y >> sigma_A) serves as an internal mechanical backstop that rectifies MPZ progenitor addition into unidirectional posterior elongation and preserves left-right symmetry; N-cadherin (cdh2) knockdown expands phi_ECS > 14%, unjamming the PSM, slowing elongation, and inducing bilateral body-axis asymmetry.; reconstructed_in_script: Continuous posterior-to-anterior active-foam & Bingham viscoplastic solver across x in [0, 300] um (`solve_ap_jamming_profile`, r_sigma_y = 0.9989, r_kT1 = 0.9922, jamming crossover x* = 81.0 um) and 2D U-shaped tailbud cellular flow simulator across 5 experimental regimes (WT Control, cdh2 Morphant, Blebbistatin Myosin-II Inhibition, SU5402 FGFR Inhibition, and Uniform-Fluid Zero-Backstop Ablation; v_elong r = 0.9717, L-R asymmetry r = 0.9851). | Nuclear-seeded Voronoi tessellation and regional interstitial space segmentation of the Danio rerio posterior tailbud lightsheet micrograph (`zebrafish_tailbud_psm_specimen.jpg`, IDR0051, N = 391 nuclei, <z> = 5.88, AP compaction r = 0.9915).; transfer_boundary: 2D dorsal-ventral optical-plane projection of the 3D U-shaped zebrafish posterior tailbud and paraxial presomitic mesoderm.; does_not_claim: Does not model 3D notochord vacuolation turgor mechanics or anterior somite epithelialization clefting.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 2D active-foam tailbud jamming gradient to 3D fibronectin extracellular matrix boundary friction (Dray et al. 2013 Current Biology 23:1335-1341) and anterior Her1/Her7 segmentation clock wavefront arrest." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.914"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

